WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.567
-Sadie, thanks for coming back
to the show.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.067
I have to talk
"Stranger Things" with you.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.534
By the way, I think this is --

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.467
I mean, it's a lot on you,
from what I've seen, so far,

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.300
but I want to get
into all that stuff.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.400
First, you're originally
from Texas, correct?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.467
-Yep.
-But you got your start

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.067
on Broadway here
in New York City.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.634
-Yeah.
-That's fantastic.
How did that happen?

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.534
-It was never really
supposed to happen.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.067
Yeah, born in a small town
in Texas.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.934
My parents are both teachers

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.934
and my dad was also
the high school football coach,

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.634
so it was kind of
very much living

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.734
in like the
"Friday Night Lights"...

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.601
[ Laughter ]
-Wow!
-...Texas Forever,
kind of world.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:34.667
-Do you have brothers?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.834
-Yeah, I have three
older brothers

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.667
and a little sister.
It's a little big family.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.701
-Were they on the football team
and stuff, the brothers?

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.267
-The older one,
the two oldest were.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.934
-[Both] Yeah.
-And no one into acting,

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:43.734
in your whole family?

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.167
-No, my my brother Mitchell,

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:47.434
who's like closest in age
with me,

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:50.901
we just started acting together
and I think we were like

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.133
on our eighth at-home production
of "Wicked" --

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.167
-At home?

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.834
-Oh, yeah, like two-man show.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.200
[ Laughter ]
He was always Glinda.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.367
I was Elphaba.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.968
-And perform for parties or...?

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.701
-No, just like our parents

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:06.801
[ Laughter ]
-Wow!
and that was it.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.467
-I love that.
-And we did everything.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.067
Not just "Wicked,"
like everything.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.334
-Yeah, we were just speaking
about --

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:13.767
-Oh, yeah,
well, that was later on.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.133
-But look at you.
You're Annie.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.400
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.934
-How cute is that?
Come on.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:18.934
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Ugh.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.467
-Now, how old are you?

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:24.667
-I think 11 or 10.
Yeah, 10 or 11.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.200
[ Laughter ]
And that was

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.067
when I started working
professionally.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.467
-Oh, yes, of course.
-Yes.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.100
-You know,
we were talking about you.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.334
We had Taylor Swift on the show
and we were talking

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.200
about her short film
to her song "All Too Well."

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.200
-Yes.
-And you're fantastic in it.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.234
-Oh, thank you.

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:40.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.100
Thank you.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.634
-And Taylor was saying
that she wasn't going

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.067
to make it,
if you didn't star in it.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:50.601
She really wanted you to star
in this film.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:51.801
Have you known each other?

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.634
-No! Like I didn't know
she knew I existed.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:57.667
[ Laughter ]
And I think, if she would've
asked me to like be a tree

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.133
in something,

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.801
[ Laughter ]
then I would've said yes
like in a heartbeat.

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.968
-Yeah. I want to be a tree
in a Taylor --

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.634
[ Laughter ]
-That would be amazing,
of course.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.234
-Taylor, if you're watching,
I'm such a good tree.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.100
-Put them in.
It's your track, yeah.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.667
-Is she good, as a director?

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:12.968
-Amazing!
-She is, right?

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.834
-Amazing. And this was kind of
like her first time

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.667
really directing actors.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.200
And she's --
Obviously, I mean,

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.634
she can do anything, so,
she was incredible at it.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.601
-You know, it turns out, though,
it wasn't the first time

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.400
that you met Taylor Swift.
-Oh, no.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.901
[ Laughter ]
-I was going to see
if you remembered.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:27.667
Do you remember this moment
right here?
-Yes!

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.968
[ Awws ]
I was so upset

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:33.000
because my eyes were like
halfway closed

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.901
and I look like I was like --
I looked like a drunk child.

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:38.400
[ Laughter ]
-No, you did not.
-I left and I was like,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.100
"Oh, I blew it! I blew it!"
-No, you look cute! Wait.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.601
How did you meet Taylor Swift,
though?

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:43.667
[ Laughter ]
Explain this to me.
-That was at her concert.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.167
I like knew someone
who could like

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.868
get me into a meet and greet.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.501
-Oh, my gosh.
-It was a big moment.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.234
But I was so upset.
-Yeah, but then, now you --

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.734
-Now, yeah, it is.
-Now you know each other.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.067
-It's fine now, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:56.701
Let's talk "Stranger Things,"
okay?

00:02:56.701 --> 00:03:00.200
Volume 1, Season 4 premieres
this Friday on Netflix.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.000
-I know, finally!

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.000
-I know. Can't wait for it.
-Yeah.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.534
Your character, Max --

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.100
what can everyone expect
from the show?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.100
What can you tell us?
-I mean, it's

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.400
darker and scarier than ever.
-It is.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.634
-The kids are obviously like
we're a lot more mature now,

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:18.801
so the show has kind of matured
with it, in a way.

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:20.801
And Max, you know,
she's not doing too hot.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.734
You're kind of getting to see
her in like her emo phase a bit.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.234
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.801
-And I don't want to say
that was like fun to explore,

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.000
but it was like a nice
like challenge.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.767
-Yeah. The early reviews,
people are saying

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:34.033
this might be the best season
of "Stranger Things"

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:35.300
because it's just so well done.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.133
There's a new character.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:39.300
Explain who this person is.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:39.968
-[ Sigh ]

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.033
That's -- Okay.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:42.334
[ Laughter ]
-Vecna.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.534
-That is Vecna.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.834
I can't say much about Vecna.
-Okay.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:46.767
-But --

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.000
-Can I ask a question?
-Yes.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.334
-Is this CGI Vecna

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:51.434
[ Laughter ]
or is this a human being?

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:54.400
-So, there's actually like
that's all practical effects,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.300
so like there's an actor
in there.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.300
-There is? Okay, good.
-Yeah.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.734
-I didn't know that.
I was like looking.

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:02.334
-So, yeah, it's all practical.
Like they had someone...

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:03.534
-Wow!
-there.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:05.267
-Fantastic.
-Like nine hours of prosthetics

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:06.968
or something.
-Is it frightening to act

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.801
opposite this thing?

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:10.300
-Yeah, but then --

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.100
In the moment, yes,
but then, in between takes,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.367
he'd be like eating
a Chick-fil-A sandwich, so.

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:18.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.367
Kind of took the magic away.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:22.467
-Vecna wants a spicy
chicken sandwich, yeah.

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.567
[ Laughter ]
Get Vecna.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.801
Then, the Internet is kind of
going crazy about --

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.100
No one knows what to say
about this,

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.868
but this is just
on the Internet.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.334
-[ Clapping ] I'm so close
to the finish line.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.868
Like I have not
spoiled anything.
-"Jimmy Fallon,

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.000
don't mess this up for me."
-I'm sprinting to the finish.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.601
-I won't mess this up for you.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:41.033
But are you --

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:43.300
-I appear...to be...
-Okay. Don't say anything.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.801
Alright, don't.
-in the air.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.033
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, you appear to be

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.334
in the air.
Let's just say that, okay.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:51.434
What was it like filming this?
-It was fun. I had fun.

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:52.667
I'm not scared of heights
or anything, so.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.334
-So you really were in the air?
-I was.

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:55.834
And I was like I don't know.

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:57.267
I was kind of like reenacting.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:00.167
I was living my like Cathy Rigby
"Peter Pan" fantasy for a bit.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:01.901
[ Laughter ]
I'm a theater kid.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.767
Like what are you going to do?
Like I had --

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.400
-You were doing "Peter Pan"
while up in the wires?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.467
-Yeah, it was just like
a little bit.

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:09.234
[ Laughter ]
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:11.801
Here's our pal Sadie Sink
in "Stranger Things."

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.868
Take a look at this.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:19.601
-How's your mom holding up?
-She's fine.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:23.234
I mean, she hates our new place,
which is like...

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:28.033
Yeah. It's terrible,
but she's fine.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:30.267
-Is she still drinking?

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:34.467
-Like -- Yeah, a little, but...

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:38.467
Well, she's working two jobs,
so it's not easy.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:41.968
-It must not be easy for you
either with your stepdad gone.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.434
-It's kind of better.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:46.200
-Are you sleeping better?

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.200
-Yeah, fine.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.801
-So no more headaches?

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.200
Nightmares?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.167
-Ooh!

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.501
Sadie Sink, everybody!

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.067
Volume 1 of season 4
of "Stranger Things"

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:03.901
premieres this Friday
on Netflix.

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:06.467
Congrats. Come back whenever.
You know we love you.

